// D&D's Feather Fall grants full fall-damage immunity to up to five falling
// allies. No BuffKind targets fall damage or DamageSource::Falling specifically,
// and nothing modifies fall speed (checked common/src/comp/buff.rs in full).
// Fall damage IS gated by armor damage_reduction reaching exactly 1.0
// (common/src/combat.rs's DamageSource::Falling branch zeroes damage only at
// that threshold), which Invulnerability already provides via
// BuffEffect::DamageReduction(1.0) (common/src/comp/buff.rs). Used here at a
// short (8s) duration -- just long enough to cover a fall, not a general
// damage-immunity grant -- as the closest available primitive. Flagged as a
// deviation: broader than pure fall immunity for its short window (blocks all
// damage sources, not falling specifically), and `strength` is a no-op per
// Invulnerability's own doc comment ("Strength does not affect this buff").
// Same ally-touch delivery shape as gravesong/bless.ron (BasicAura, InGroup);
// aoe stays None like every other BasicAura spell -- the AoE radius is the
// `range` field itself, not a separate compendium aoe shape.
BasicAura(
    buildup_duration: 0.5,
    cast_duration: 0.3,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    targets: InGroup,
    auras: [
        (
            kind: Invulnerability,
            strength: 0.0,
            duration: Some(8.0),
            category: Some(Magical),
        ),
    ],
    aura_duration: Some(1.0),
    range: 18.0,
    energy_cost: 45.0,
    scales_with_combo: false,
    specifier: None,
    meta: (school: Some(Transmutation), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
